  "authoringNote": "The policy input is the frozen negative input pinned by hash, whose bytes equal the reviewed v2 pack except packId lab-k0823-jd-20261018-v2-unreviewed and reviewedAsOf null. The case policyPackId equals that packId, so R08.pack_id_differs does not hold; the date 2026-10-18 is supported and equals the argument. reviewedAsOf is null, so R08 holds R08.pack_unreviewed: missing for the administrative reviewer with the scope_hold effect, naming no document, and the state is scope_hold. The input still lists its source references, so R08.pack_unsourced does not hold. Rules, conditions and conventions are identical to the reviewed pack, so every other finding is as for the supported packet; R01 passes citing the eight supplier and order item code facts. Every other finding follows the supported packet, checked by hand: the final encounter (2026-08-26) and final signed order (2026-09-04) name practitioner identifier SYN-PRAC-0001, and the order is after the encounter and within the C01 bound 2027-02-26; the receipt references the order version and is recorded at 2026-09-05T18:40:00Z, after the C06 span 2026-09-03T10:00:00Z to 2026-09-05T12:00:00Z of the date-only order; the named supplier record is usable and hash-valid. R02 passes with six beneficiary citations (encounter, order, receipt), R03 passes with nine, R04 with six (status, date and practitioner identifier of each final document; null times supply no fact), R05 with four. R06 stays manual_review for the qualified clinical reviewer with R06.clinical_review and the five full /clinical/ pointers; it neither blocks nor satisfies readiness and draws no medical necessity conclusion. R07 passes citing the stated LCMP flag false; no ATP, specialty, home assessment or proof-of-delivery item is required. R09 passes. R10 is not_applicable with R10.pure_assessment. Quarantine and superseded lists are empty and clinicalReviewRequired is true. Parent affectedDocuments are empty: no held condition is restricted, unreadable or failed provenance (C07).",
